{"strongs": "H3322", "word": "יָצַג", "translit": "ya.tsag", "root": "יצג", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb Hiph`il", "gloss": "set, place", "definition": "[ יָצַג ] verb Hiph`il set, place , a vivid and forcible synonym of שָׂם ( Kö i. 430 Ges «GKC:71»§ 71 ) — Hiph`il Perfect suffix הִצִּיגַּ֫נִי Jer 51:34 Qr ( Kt הציגנו ), Job 17:6 1 singular suffix הִצַּגְתִּיו Gen 43:9 וְהִצַּגְּתִּיהָ consecutive Hos 2:5 Imperfect וַיַּצֵּג Gen 30:38 ; Judg 8:27 suffix וַיַּצִּגֵם Gen 47:2 2 masculine singular תַּצִּיג Judg 7:5 , etc.; Imperative הַצִּ֫יגוּ Amos 5:15 Infinitive construct הַצֵּג Deut 28:56 ( Ges «GKC:53»§ 53 , 3, R.2 Kö l.c .); Participle מַצִּיג Judg 6:37 — set, place , with accusative: + ב location Gen 30:28 ( J ; + לְֹנכַח צאֹן ), Judg 6:37 ; Judg 8:27 ; 2Sam 6:17 ( + בְּתוֺךְ ), with בְּתוֺךְ in || 1Chr 16:1 + אֵצֶל 1Sam 5:2 of setting foot on ( לְ ) ground Deut 28:56 ; Gen 33:15 ( J ; followed by עִם ) = station with thee some of my retinue; + לִפְנֵי Gen 43:9 ( J ); so with idea of presenting, introducing to Gen 47:2 ( J ); set (so that all may see) + לְ Job 17:6 followed by 2 accusative ( = set as ) Jer 51:34 וְהִצַּגְתִּיהָ כְּיוֺם הִוָָּֽלְדָ֑הּ Hos 2:5 and (lest) I set ( = exhibit ) her as in the day when she was born (|| אַפְשִׁיטֶנָּה עֲרֻמָּה ); figurative set up, establish , הציגר בשׁער משׁפט Amos 5:15 (opposed to v Amos 5:7 לארץ הניחו ). Hoph`al Imperfect יצָֻּ֑ג Exod 10:24 ( E ) be stayed, stopped, detained (of herds, etc.) יִצִהָר , יִצְחָק , יִצְחָר see below צהר , צהק , צחר", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3666')\">BDB3666</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3322')\">H3322</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3665')\">BDB3665</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3667')\">BDB3667</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>יָצַג</bdbheb>] <b>verb Hiph`il</b> <highlightword>set, place</highlightword>, a vivid and forcible synonym of <bdbheb>שָׂם</bdbheb> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kö')\">Kö<sup>i. 430</su